## Main Narrative Summary 
### Marien's Room
Upon returning to her room, Marien removes Sona to enjoy a brief moment of quiet solitude while unpacking her belongings. Before heading out for her nighttime expedition with Hanino, Marien faces a choice regarding a lost bee hovering over a piece of chocolate near her window:
- Choice A (Call Her Daughter): Marien puts Sona back on to call her daughter. They chat about Marien's adventurous start at the Silver Center, and her daughter reveals she secretly packed an old Y2K-era digital camera in Marien's bag—noting that outdated tech lacking AI or modern chips might survive the upcoming solar storms.

- Choice B (Help the Bee): Marien opts not to call and instead tries to guide the lost bee outside. After trying various methods (mimicking vibrations, moving the chocolate, and dimming the lights), she mimics the mournful cry of the Entity (기이이이—). Recognizing the vibration, the bee takes flight and exits through the open window into the night.

Looking outside, Marien notices a surreal purple aurora rippling across the dark sky. With the time reading 9:40 PM—nearing her 10:00 PM meeting with Hanino—she puts Sona back on, secures the Entity's tiger-patterned feather onto her energy-charging bracelet, and packs her gear into her backpack:
- Energy-Charging Bracelet with the Entity's Feather
- Yassin's Flashlight
- Rented Biotech Device
- Y2K Digital Camera (if she called her daughter)


### Forest
Marien and Heka cross the night garden to meet Hanino at the main entrance. Finding the area clear of Yassin, they join to Hanino, but Hanino immediately leads them into the pitch-black forest with surprising speed. As the dense canopy blocks out the sky, Hanino vanishes into the dark ahead.
To keep from getting lost on the unfamiliar path, Marien instructs Sona to track Hanino’s trail by combining Heka’s olfactory data with real-time audio amplification of Hanino's distant, jingling staff. Guided by Heka’s nose, Marien presses forward through the humid night until they arrive at the chilly, mist-shrouded entrance of the forest cave.

### Cave
Upon reaching the chilly cave entrance, Marien utilizes her gear to navigate the pitch-black space alongside Heka. Depending on her starting equipment:
- Vintage Digital Camera: Marien flashes a cold, brilliant light into the void, momentarily revealing frozen lava formations on the ceiling, hanging tree roots, and damp, glistening walls in the camera's viewfinder.
- Quantum Dot Lenses / Shield Glasses / Actuator Belt / Bipedal Modules / Medical Strap / Diamond grillz: Each specialized augment aids her stability, vision, or physical stamina, allowing her to push deep into the treacherous cave despite Sona’s persistent biological telemetry alerts.

Further inside, near the ashes of a recent campfire, Marien discovers three items and makes her choice: Choice Outcome: Marien picks up the Dynamo Stone (or alternative item) and stows it securely in her backpack.

Suddenly, Sona amplifies a chanted ritual echoing from deep within the cave. The eerie chant speaks of the primeval night, two suns, and the collapsing boundaries between humans, beasts, and quantum code. Following the chant and guided by the Entity's tiger-patterned feather—which breaks free from her snapped bracelet and floats gracefully along the cave’s air currents—Marien and Heka reach a dead-end chamber where Hanino is chanting before an ancient wall.

The feather comes to rest over a ancient petroglyph carved into the rock: The Petroglyph's Imagery: Two suns rise over a calm lake—the left sun harboring a three-legged bird, the right harboring nine small birds. A queen bee leads a swarm northward, while half-human, half-dog figures worship the suns, one playing a flute crafted from bird bone.

Marien confronts Hanino, initiating a multi-part conversation:
- On Why Marien Was Chosen: Hanino admits she deliberately guided Marien here because Marien's body is relatively unaugmented and "pure," free of machine noise, and because Heka signaled Marien's longing for real adventure.
- On the Omen: Hanino explains that when the two suns align, all boundaries will melt into chaos. She asks if Marien can hear the "speech of bees" or the "sound of the bone flute," warning that only those who master these ancient sounds will understand the coming storm.
- Recording the Discovery (Vintage Camera): Marien captures clear digital photos of the petroglyph and its sacred figures under her camera's flash to preserve proof.

Overwhelmed by exhaustion, Marien checks the time via Sona—it is 2:34 AM. Ignoring Sona's health warnings regarding sleep deprivation, Marien bids farewell to Hanino, who chooses to stay behind and listen to the stone's breath. Half-asleep, Marien and Heka make their way back out of the damp cave and return through the forest gates to the Silver Center.

### Marien's Room
Marien stumbles through her room door, exhausted. Lacking the energy to remove Sona, she collapses onto her unmade bed, barely kicking off her shoes. Heka crawls onto the mattress beside her legs, curling up with a soft, steady snore. With the vivid image of the cave's petroglyphs lingering behind her eyelids, Marien sinks into a deep, heavy sleep.

